cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PHON in your research, please cite this repository."
title: "PHON: A Domain-Specific Language for Photonic and Phononic Wave Simulation with Neural Network Inference"
abstract: >-
  PHON is an open-source DSL for photonic and phononic circuit design and neural network inference. A single source compiles to simulation, GDSII layout export, and neural network inference via layer/propagate primitives with numpy-backed matmul.
  As of v0.10.1, PHON natively supports both photonic (optical) and phononic (acoustic) media through a unified `medium kind` attribute, dispatching physics constants (refractive index, sound velocity) without changing the computation, enabling cross-medium weight transfer.
  v0.10.1 simulates on CPU; physical deployment (photonic chips, SAW devices) is future work.
  Phase 6 (v0.11.0) adds MZI (Mach-Zehnder Interferometer) optical simulation and SVD-based mesh generation. Phase 5 (v0.10.0) achieves 97.78% MNIST test accuracy with 0 mismatches versus scikit-learn predictions on a 100-sample audit set. The test suite includes 184 passing tests.
